RESULT
  Internal DHCP server ..... PASS   pre-auth client gets a lease from the on-box DHCP server
                                    (DISCOVER/OFFER/REQUEST/ACK; binding installed)
  Web authentication ....... PASS   unauth HTTP is intercepted/redirected to the portal;
                                    portal login authorises the port; traffic then forwards
  (The case body in ck.db is just "Refer to 4.3.1.doc" - the procedure below is a faithful
   reconstruction exercising the two named features on the IE520.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUT / authenticator + DHCP server : u4  S/N 264A23052  MAC 84e3.2787.09c0
  Client / supplicant : tb470 eth2  MAC 00:f0:4d:00:77:17  -> u4 port1.0.2 (access vlan60,
                        auth-web enabled).  Static 10.10.60.20 used for the web-auth HTTP;
                        the DHCP lease is proven separately with a scapy DHCP transaction.
  Through-port target : u5  vlan60 SVI 10.10.60.3  (via u4<->u5 vlan60 trunk).
  RADIUS + DHCP + portal are all ON THE IE520 (no external servers).

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA / browser needed. The internal DHCP server is exercised with a scapy DHCP
  Discover/Request (so the host's own routing is untouched). Web-auth is exercised with curl
  from the host: fetch the portal, show the 307 interception of ordinary HTTP, POST the
  credentials of a local-RADIUS user, and confirm the port authorises. Functional test.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG APPLIED   (running-config only, NOT saved to startup)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4#
  aaa authentication auth-web default group radius
  radius-server local
   server enable
   nas 127.0.0.1 key localkey
   user webuser password webpass
  radius-server host 127.0.0.1 key localkey
  auth-web-server ipaddress 10.10.60.1
  service dhcp-server
  ip dhcp pool authpool
   network 10.10.60.0/27
   range 10.10.60.10 10.10.60.15
   default-router 10.10.60.1
   lease 0 1 0
  interface vlan60   ip address 10.10.60.1/27
  interface port1.0.2
   switchport mode access ; switchport access vlan 60
   auth-web enable

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART A - Internal DHCP Server (serves the pre-authenticated client)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
>>> host: DHCP DISCOVER (src MAC 00:f0:4d:00:77:17, xid 0x33445566)
<<< DHCP OFFER  yiaddr=10.10.60.10  server_id=10.10.60.1  router=10.10.60.1  mask=255.255.255.224  lease=3600s
>>> host: DHCP REQUEST for 10.10.60.10
<<< DHCP ACK  yiaddr=10.10.60.10  (lease confirmed)

u4# show ip dhcp binding
Pool authpool Network 10.10.60.0/27
IP address       Client Id / Hardware address        Type     Lease expires
10.10.60.10      00f0.4d00.7717                       Dynamic  9 Sep 2026 03:40:31
  => the IE520's internal DHCP server offered, acknowledged and bound a lease to the client
     while the port is still unauthenticated (web-auth permits DHCP pre-auth). PASS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART B - Web Authentication (intercept -> portal -> authorise)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- pre-auth: the port blocks through traffic --
host# ping -I 10.10.60.20 10.10.60.3 (u5)      -> 2 transmitted, 0 received, 100% packet loss

-- unauthenticated HTTP is intercepted and redirected to the portal --
host# curl -i http://10.10.60.3/            (an ordinary through-port HTTP request)
HTTP/1.1 307 Moved Temporarily
Location: http://10.10.60.1/

-- the portal serves the login page --
host# curl -i http://10.10.60.1/
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
...
<FORM action="http://10.10.60.1/index.cgi" name="AUTH" method="POST">
  <INPUT ... name="USERNAME">
  <INPUT type="password" name="PASSWORD">
  <INPUT type="submit" name="ACTION" value="login">

-- submit the local-RADIUS user's credentials --
host# curl -d "USERNAME=webuser&PASSWORD=webpass&ACTION=login" http://10.10.60.1/index.cgi
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
<STRONG>Web Access Authentication Gateway</STRONG>
Authenticating - Server Based User Authentication in progress ...

u4# show auth interface port1.0.2
  portStatus: Authorized                <-- web authentication succeeded
  authWeb: enabled

-- post-auth: the same traffic now forwards --
host# ping -I 10.10.60.20 10.10.60.3 (u5)      -> 3 transmitted, 3 received, 0% packet loss
  => the client, given an address by the internal DHCP server, was redirected to the on-box
     web-auth portal, authenticated against the local RADIUS user, and the port moved to
     Authorized - after which through traffic forwards. PASS.
